      "note": "power/standby key (service manual: M1 reads POWER SW and M2 relays it as RX bit (5,4); the app's PowerManager handles button object 14: press aborts each standby receiver, release asks each to go to standby). Measured by hwsuite HW-09: a short press unmounts the USB stick at once (SP16_USB unmounted_by_app=yes, LED off), latches TX 0x67 bit 0 (the app's 'transition Standby' flag, after which a real unit's M1 cuts power) and, until the next start, project saves hang at SAVING 0%; so it runs last. The emulator has no M1, so the app stays in standby until it restarts"
    }
